M10_CH08_STD_501	M10_CH08	Advanced Identity Proof 1	Standard	Prove that: (tan θ / (1 - cot θ)) + (cot θ / (1 - tan θ)) = 1 + sec θ cosec θ.	{"rubric": "Convert to sin and cos. LHS = sin^2 θ / (cos θ (sin θ - cos θ)) - cos^2 θ / (sin θ (sin θ - cos θ)) = (sin^3 θ - cos^3 θ) / (sin θ cos θ (sin θ - cos θ)) = 1 + sec θ cosec θ."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
M10_CH08_STD_502	M10_CH08	Advanced Identity Proof 2	Standard	Prove that: (cos A - sin A + 1) / (cos A + sin A - 1) = cosec A + cot A using identity cosec^2 A = 1 + cot^2 A.	{"rubric": "Divide by sin A => (cot A - 1 + cosec A) / (cot A + 1 - cosec A). Substitute 1 = cosec^2 A - cot^2 A in numerator and factorize."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
M10_CH08_STD_503	M10_CH08	Elimination of Parameter	Standard	If x = a sec θ + b tan θ and y = a tan θ + b sec θ, prove that x^2 - y^2 = a^2 - b^2.	{"rubric": "x^2 - y^2 = (a sec θ + b tan θ)^2 - (a tan θ + b sec θ)^2. Expand and group terms: a^2(sec^2 θ - tan^2 θ) - b^2(sec^2 θ - tan^2 θ) = a^2 - b^2."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
