M10_CH09_STD_401	M10_CH09	Light House Case Study	Standard	As observed from the top of a 75 m high lighthouse from the sea-level, the angles of depression of two ships are 30° and 45°. If one ship is exactly behind the other on the same side of the lighthouse, find the distance between the two ships.	{"rubric": "tan 45° = 75 / x => x = 75 m. tan 30° = 75 / (x + d) => 1/√3 = 75 / (75 + d) => d = 75(√3 - 1) m."}	4.0	Case_Study	Apply	Medium	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
