M10_CH13_STD_501	M10_CH13	Missing Frequencies Median	Standard	The median of the following data is 525. Find the values of x and y, if the total frequency is 100. Classes: 0-100 (2), 100-200 (5), 200-300 (x), 300-400 (12), 400-500 (17), 500-600 (20), 600-700 (y), 700-800 (9), 800-900 (7), 900-1000 (4).	{"rubric": "Median class = 500-600. l=500, f=20, cf=36+x, h=100. 525 = 500 + [(50 - (36+x))/20]*100 => 25 = (14-x)*5 => 14-x = 5 => x = 9. Since sum = 76+x+y = 100 => y = 15."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
M10_CH13_STD_502	M10_CH13	Missing Frequency Mean	Standard	The mean of the following frequency distribution is 18. The frequency f in class 19-21 is missing. Find f. Classes: 11-13 (7), 13-15 (6), 15-17 (9), 17-19 (13), 19-21 (f), 21-23 (5), 23-25 (4).	{"rubric": "x_i: 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24. Sum f_i*x_i = 752 + 20f. Sum f_i = 44 + f. 18 * (44 + f) = 752 + 20f => 792 + 18f = 752 + 20f => 2f = 40 => f = 20."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
M10_CH13_STD_503	M10_CH13	Full Table Median Calculation	Standard	A life insurance agent found the following data for age distribution of 100 policy holders. Calculate the median age. Ages: Below 20 (2), Below 25 (6), Below 30 (24), Below 35 (45), Below 40 (78), Below 45 (89), Below 50 (92), Below 55 (98), Below 60 (100).	{"rubric": "Convert to class intervals: 15-20 (2), 20-25 (4), 25-30 (18), 30-35 (21), 35-40 (33), 40-45 (11)... Median class = 35-40. l=35, cf=45, f=33, h=5. Median = 35 + [(50-45)/33]*5 = 35 + 25/33 = 35.76 years."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
M10_CH13_STD_504	M10_CH13	Comparative Mean and Median	Standard	The length of 40 leaves of a plant are measured correct to nearest millimeter: 118-126 (3), 127-135 (5), 136-144 (9), 145-153 (12), 154-162 (5), 163-171 (4), 172-180 (2). Find median length of leaves.	{"rubric": "Continuous classes: 117.5-126.5 (3), 126.5-135.5 (5), 135.5-144.5 (9), 144.5-153.5 (12)... N/2 = 20. Median class = 144.5-153.5. l=144.5, cf=17, f=12, h=9. Median = 144.5 + [(20-17)/12]*9 = 144.5 + 2.25 = 146.75 mm."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
