M10_CH14_STD_501	M10_CH14	Card Game Complex Removal	Standard	All the jacks, queens and kings are removed from a deck of 52 cards. The remaining cards are well shuffled and a card is drawn. Find probability of getting: (i) a black face card (ii) a red card (iii) a 10 (iv) a picture card.	{"rubric": "Face cards removed = 12. Remaining total = 40. (i) Black face card = 0/40 = 0. (ii) Red cards remaining = 20/40 = 1/2. (iii) Tens remaining = 4/40 = 1/10. (iv) Picture cards remaining = 0/40 = 0."}	5.0	Cat_A	Analyze	Hard	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
