M10_CH14_STD_503	M10_CH14	Three Coins Toss All Cases	Standard	Three coins are tossed simultaneously. Find the probability of getting: (i) exactly 2 heads (ii) at least 2 heads (iii) at most 2 heads (iv) no heads.	{"rubric": "Total = 8 {HHH, HHT, HTH, THH, HTT, THT, TTH, TTT}. (i) Exactly 2 heads = 3/8. (ii) At least 2 heads {HHH, HHT, HTH, THH} = 4/8 = 1/2. (iii) At most 2 heads = 7/8. (iv) No heads {TTT} = 1/8."}	5.0	Cat_A	Apply	Medium	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
M10_CH14_STD_504	M10_CH14	Box Disc Number Properties	Standard	A box contains 90 discs which are numbered from 1 to 90. If one disc is drawn at random, find probability that it bears: (i) a two-digit number (ii) a perfect square number (iii) a number divisible by 5.	{"rubric": "Total = 90. (i) Two-digit (10 to 90) = 81 => 81/90 = 9/10. (ii) Perfect squares {1,4,9,16,25,36,49,64,81} = 9 => 9/90 = 1/10. (iii) Divisible by 5 (5,10...90) = 18 => 18/90 = 1/5."}	5.0	Cat_A	Apply	Medium	\N	[]	\N	t	\N	\N	f	MATH	All India
