SCI_2018_D_04	S10_CH06	\N	Standard (041)	The breakdown of pyruvate to give carbon dioxide, water, and energy takes place in:\r\n(A) Cytoplasm\r\n(B) Mitochondria\r\n(C) Chloroplast\r\n(D) Nucleus	{"answer": "1 Mark for Option (B)"}	1.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	723d41ce292fdc49e59995ca56bfb8cddfa7464062cd961aea6bdba7cf2a2b40	[]	Correct Option: (B)\r\nAerobic respiration, involving the Krebs cycle and oxidative phosphorylation of pyruvate, occurs within the mitochondria.	t	2018	Delhi Set 1	f	SCI	Delhi
