SST_2024_AI_05	SS10_ECO_01	\N	Standard (041)	Why is the issue of sustainability central to development? Support with one example of ground water exploitation in India.	{"concept": "1 Mark", "example": "1 Mark"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	d9bfe332afa21f5fd76703e7cc847caefa1913abc1c1ba838cda4f1f0eec2837	[]	Development must satisfy current human needs without compromising the ecological capital of future generations. In India, over one-third of districts are over-pumping groundwater (e.g. Punjab and Western UP tube-wells), lowering aquifers by over 4 meters and threatening long-term food security.	t	2024	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2024_AI_06	SS10_POL_02	\N	Standard (041)	State any two features of the language policy adopted by the Indian Constitution to preserve national federal harmony.	{"feature1": "1 Mark", "feature2": "1 Mark"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	f0ecbf4183675ed7beb290b728026fd0c98cfa2dbae110719003a855a53303ca	[]	1. No National Language: Hindi is designated as an official language, but not granted national language status to protect non-Hindi states.\r\n2. Scheduled Languages: The Eighth Schedule recognizes 22 languages; candidates taking central exams may write in any scheduled language.	t	2024	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2024_AI_07	SS10_GEO_02	\N	Standard (041)	Mention any two institutional reforms initiated by the Government of India in the agricultural sector after independence.	{"reform1": "1 Mark", "reform2": "1 Mark"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	b6dd6cb9d4b04bce2caa3c14513cc5f0ecc9b286ec96c6c792325c96919aa64f	[]	1. Abolition of Zamindari: Abolished feudal land intermediaries and consolidated fragmented land holdings.\r\n2. Comprehensive Crop Insurance: Introduced insurance covering droughts, floods, and pests, supported by Grameen Banks and Kisan Credit Cards (KCC).	t	2024	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
