SST_2023_D_05	SS10_ECO_01	\N	Standard (041)	Why is per capita income alone insufficient to assess national human development? State two limitations.	{"limitation1": "1 Mark", "limitation2": "1 Mark"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	34fbdd09c62025917525a433c77e7a50bdfac1da4e273063603e63daf0d8a9ff	[]	1. Disregards Income Distribution: High average per capita income can conceal wealth concentration where the majority remains impoverished.\r\n2. Ignores Human Capabilities: It does not measure essential welfare factors such as infant mortality rates, public health access, literacy, and environmental security.	t	2023	Delhi Set 1	f	SST	Delhi
