PYQ_2024_BASIC_SET1_Q05	M10_CH03	Solving Linear System by Elimination	Basic	Solve the pair of linear equations:\r\n$$x + y = 14$$\r\n$$x - y = 4$$	[{"step": "Add equations: (x + y) + (x - y) = 14 + 4 => 2x = 18 => x = 9", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "Substitute x = 9 into first equation: 9 + y = 14 => y = 5", "marks": 1.0}]	2.0	Short Answer	Applying	Easy	\N	["CBSE_2024", "Basic_241", "Set_1", "Section_B"]	Given system:\r\n$$x + y = 14 \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$$\r\n$$x - y = 4 \\quad \\text{--- (2)}$$\r\nAdding equation (1) and equation (2):\r\n$$2x = 18 \\implies x = 9$$\r\nSubstitute $x = 9$ into (1):\r\n$$9 + y = 14 \\implies y = 14 - 9 = 5.$$\r\nTherefore, $x = 9$ and $y = 5$.	t	2024	Basic Set 1	t	MATH	All India
