SST_2023_AI_08	SS10_HIS_01	\N	Standard (041)	Explain the concept of 'Liberal Nationalism' in 19th-century Europe in political and economic spheres.	{"economic": "1.5 Marks", "political": "1.5 Marks"}	3.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	013ec599674149f26a81d16602cb71ca2d86f981ac413ec3ab78614a2c25b201	[]	1. Political Sphere: Emphasized governance by consent, constitutional representation, parliamentary supremacy, and the termination of monarchical privileges.\r\n2. Economic Sphere: Advocated for freedom of domestic markets, unrestricted movement of goods and capital, and the removal of internal state tariff barriers.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2023_AI_09	SS10_ECO_02	\N	Standard (041)	Explain the role played by the public sector in nation-building and socioeconomic development in India.	{"regional": "1 Mark", "subsidies": "1 Mark", "infrastructure": "1 Mark"}	3.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	3c2dec6ce18cc208a2a4af583f407e98e4af3a79015167715297b0f20d740e4c	[]	1. Heavy Infrastructure Investment: Capital projects (railways, power generation, defense) with long gestation periods require government financing.\r\n2. Balanced Regional Growth: Locating steel plants and heavy industrial units in backward tribal areas promotes regional balance.\r\n3. Basic Welfare Subsidies: Distributing foodgrains through PDS and supplying public water and electricity below commercial cost supports low-income populations.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2023_AI_10	SS10_POL_03	\N	Standard (041)	How do caste inequalities persist in modern India despite constitutional bans on untouchability? State three dimensions.	{"economic": "1 Mark", "marriage": "1 Mark", "education": "1 Mark"}	3.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	e5a74ecb374cfe1e4718527c1c69fd000df7ba869bb494915646eef182c017ed	[]	1. Socioeconomic Correlation: Upper-caste groups remain disproportionately represented in higher-income brackets, while Scheduled Castes face higher poverty rates.\r\n2. Educational Disparities: Elite institutions show lower transition rates for marginalized communities due to historical disparities.\r\n3. Endogamous Marriage: Inter-caste marriages remain limited in practice, reinforcing caste-based networks.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2023_AI_11	SS10_ECO_03	\N	Standard (041)	Compare formal sources of credit with informal sources of credit in rural India across: (i) interest rates, (ii) supervision, (iii) collateral requirements.	{"interest": "1 Mark", "collateral": "1 Mark", "supervision": "1 Mark"}	3.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	59cdcac6a976c0bdd659ab1010098bb03916679d7299fd80875b05903b290685	[]	1. Interest Rates: Formal sources (commercial banks, cooperatives) charge lower, regulated interest rates; informal sources (moneylenders, traders) charge higher rates (30–60% per annum).\r\n2. Regulatory Supervision: Formal sources are monitored by the Reserve Bank of India; informal lenders operate without regulatory oversight.\r\n3. Collateral Requirements: Formal banks require valid documentation and collateral; informal moneylenders advance loans on personal familiarity without asset paperwork.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2023_AI_12	SS10_GEO_06	\N	Standard (041)	Classify manufacturing industries on the basis of raw materials used, with two distinct industrial examples for each category.	{"agro": "1.5 Marks", "mineral": "1.5 Marks"}	3.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	c63df0743b53b64c53658e615d0dbc2be59b69dc9cc48fdd06b719dabe899e5d	[]	1. Agro-Based Industries: Process raw materials harvested from agriculture: Cotton textiles, Jute textiles, Sugar, Edible Oils.\r\n2. Mineral-Based Industries: Use mined mineral ores and metals as feedstocks: Iron and Steel, Aluminum smelting, Cement, Chemical fertilizers.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
PYQ_2024_BASIC_SET1_Q06	M10_CH05	Calculation of Specific AP Term	Basic	Find the $12^{\\text{th}}$ term of the A.P.: $2, 7, 12, \\dots$	[{"step": "Identify first term a = 2 and common difference d = 7 - 2 = 5", "marks": 0.5}, {"step": "Apply formula a12 = a + (12 - 1)d = 2 + 11(5)", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "Compute 2 + 55 = 57", "marks": 0.5}]	2.0	Short Answer	Applying	Easy	\N	["CBSE_2024", "Basic_241", "Set_1", "Section_B"]	Here:\r\n• First term $a = 2$\r\n• Common difference $d = 7 - 2 = 5$\r\n• Number of terms $n = 12$\r\n\r\n$$a_n = a + (n - 1)d$$\r\n$$a_{12} = 2 + (12 - 1)(5)$$\r\n$$a_{12} = 2 + 11 \\times 5 = 2 + 55 = 57.$$\r\nThe $12^{\\text{th}}$ term is **57**.	t	2024	Basic Set 1	t	MATH	All India
SST_2023_AI_13	SS10_HIS_02	\N	Standard (041)	Evaluate the participation of the business class and industrial working class in the Civil Disobedience Movement of 1930.	{"workers": "2.5 Marks", "business": "2.5 Marks"}	5.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	51acfcdfc0cfbf569b026c4669f3a7991920cc4ac74adc08ee859516adb59262	[]	1. Industrial Business Class (Led by Purshottamdas Thakurdas and G.D. Birla):\r\n- Supported the movement to resist colonial currency exchange ratios (rupee-sterling ratio) and demand import tariffs against British textiles.\r\n- Formed FICCI in 1927 and provided financial backing to Congress while refusing to import foreign manufactured items.\r\n2. Industrial Working Class:\r\n- Overall participation was limited except in the Nagpur region, where workers engaged in railway and dock strikes.\r\n- Because Congress maintained close relationships with industrial capitalists, most factory laborers remained cautious.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SCI_2019_D_06	S10_CH07	\N	Standard (041)	What is a synapse? How does a nerve impulse travel across the microscopic gap between two adjacent neurons?	{"definition": "1 Mark", "neurotransmission": "1 Mark"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	1c5c27599abd805e100818799fb2f96d974fa629f8821d21c83521db373a5a51	[]	1. Synapse: The microscopic junction between the axon terminal of one neuron and the dendrite of the subsequent neuron.\r\n2. Transmission: When an electrical nerve impulse reaches the axon end, it triggers the release of chemical neurotransmitters (e.g., acetylcholine) into the synaptic cleft. These diffuse across the gap and bind to receptor sites on the next dendrite, generating a new electrical impulse.	t	2019	Delhi Set 1	f	SCI	Delhi
SST_2023_AI_14	SS10_POL_02	\N	Standard (041)	Explain the role of the independent judiciary in upholding federalism and resolving disputes between the Union and the States.	{"arbiter": "1.5 Marks", "tax_amendment": "2 Marks", "original_jurisdiction": "1.5 Marks"}	5.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	c3e391264407c678fe5acdda0dbb3c271b5dc47caf8a66cdb53e27a1ebfafc60	[]	1. Constitutional Arbiter: The Supreme Court acts as the final interpreter of the Constitution, preventing either level of government from overriding allocated powers.\r\n2. Original Dispute Jurisdiction: Article 131 grants original jurisdiction over legal disputes between the Government of India and one or more States.\r\n3. Financial and Tax Reviews: Resolves inter-state tax disputes and adjudicates revenue-sharing arrangements.\r\n4. Amendment Oversight: Enforces the basic structure doctrine, ensuring federal provisions cannot be unilaterally amended without ratification by at least half of the state legislatures.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2023_AI_15	SS10_ECO_04	\N	Standard (041)	What is Fair Globalization? State four policy interventions through which governments can ensure globalization benefits all citizens equitably.	{"fair_def": "1 Mark", "policies": "4 Marks (1 Mark each)"}	5.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	9788fbb7734d0dc34ce918dd0bfe9961ba0818d4c6a14f22effe3363d4f20c84	[]	1. Definition: A framework ensuring globalization opportunities are shared equitably and vulnerable domestic populations are protected.\r\n2. Four Policy Interventions:\r\n- Strict Labor Law Compliance: Enforce workplace safety and fair wage regulations for workers in domestic and multinational factories.\r\n- Support for Small Domestic Producers: Provide subsidized credit, technology upgrades, and infrastructure until local producers can compete globally.\r\n- Protective Trade Barriers: Use WTO-compliant tariffs and quotas to shield domestic industries from dumping.\r\n- Collective Developing Nation Bargaining: Cooperate with other developing nations in WTO negotiations to counter trade rules favoring developed economies.	t	2023	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
