SCI_2022_D_03	S10_CH09	\N	Standard (041)	In human beings, the statistical probability of a fertilized egg resulting in a male child is:\r\n(A) 25%\r\n(B) 50%\r\n(C) 75%\r\n(D) 100%	{"answer": "1 Mark for Option (B)"}	1.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	370a70b7a2d418cdcee7626dac5183a35cb7795c244b991fb351732720a76a80	[]	Correct Option: (B)\r\n50%. A female always donates an X chromosome; half of male sperms carry an X and half carry a Y chromosome (1:1 ratio).	t	2022	Delhi Set 1	f	SCI	Delhi
