SCI_2022_D_05	S10_CH04	\N	Standard (041)	Write the electron dot structure of ethane (C2H6) and ethene (C2H4). State the nature of covalent bonds present in both.	{"ethane": "1 Mark", "ethene": "1 Mark"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	25eb8df7756ebd19958ce2035f9e426a4227e84569c38390b04c7e9c8377dcec	[]	1. Ethane: H3C-CH3 contains 7 single covalent bonds (shared electron pairs).\r\n2. Ethene: H2C=CH2 contains 4 single C-H covalent bonds and 1 double C=C covalent bond (2 shared electron pairs).	t	2022	Delhi Set 1	f	SCI	Delhi
