SCI_2022_D_13	S10_CH12	\N	Standard (041)	(a) Derive the formula for equivalent resistance of three resistors R1, R2, and R3 connected in series.\r\n(b) An electric heater draws 10 A from a 220 V line for 2 hours daily. Compute its power rating and monthly electricity consumption in kWh (commercial units) for 30 days.	{"numerical": "2.5 Marks", "derivation": "2.5 Marks"}	5.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	a227ecc12980232de93150a5fede30f32642b1b6d0f29c428450d2f27b9c1b47	[]	(a) Derivation:\r\nIn series, current I remains identical through all resistors while total voltage V = V1 + V2 + V3.\r\nBy Ohm's law: V1 = I*R1, V2 = I*R2, V3 = I*R3.\r\nI*Req = I*R1 + I*R2 + I*R3 -> Req = R1 + R2 + R3.\r\n(b) Numerical:\r\nPower P = V * I = 220 V * 10 A = 2200 W = 2.2 kW.\r\nDaily Energy = 2.2 kW * 2 h = 4.4 kWh.\r\nMonthly Energy (30 days) = 4.4 * 30 = 132 kWh (commercial units).	t	2022	Delhi Set 1	f	SCI	Delhi
