SCI_2019_D_03	S10_CH03	\N	Standard (041)	Galvanisation is a method of protecting iron from rusting by coating it with a thin layer of:\r\n(A) Gallium\r\n(B) Aluminum\r\n(C) Zinc\r\n(D) Silver	{"answer": "1 Mark for Option (C)"}	1.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	c09f3c319bdb63cee3d46ad262c1a65721ef24abca0fd49185389819c117d9dd	[]	Correct Option: (C)\r\nGalvanisation coats iron or steel with a thin protective layer of metallic zinc (Zn) to prevent corrosion.	t	2019	Delhi Set 1	f	SCI	Delhi
CBSE_SQP_2025_Q13	M10_CH06	Basic Proportionality Theorem Formal Proof	Standard	State and prove Basic Proportionality Theorem (Thales Theorem).	[{"step": "Accurate statement of theorem", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "Correct geometric figure with perpendiculars EF perp AB and DG perp AC and joins BE, CD", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "Derive Area(ADE)/Area(BDE) = AD/DB", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "Derive Area(ADE)/Area(DEC) = AE/EC", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "Cite common base DE between parallel lines DE || BC => conclude AD/DB = AE/EC", "marks": 1.0}]	5.0	Word Problems	Analysing	Hard	\N	["CBSE_SQP_2025", "Official_Sample_Paper", "Section_D"]	**Statement:** If a line is drawn parallel to one side of a triangle intersecting the other two sides in distinct points, the other two sides are divided in the same ratio.\r\n\r\n**Given:** In $\\Delta ABC$, line $DE \\parallel BC$ intersects $AB$ at $D$ and $AC$ at $E$.\r\n**To Prove:** $\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC}$.\r\n**Construction:** Join $BE$ and $CD$. Draw $EF \\perp AB$ and $DG \\perp AC$.\r\n\r\n**Proof:**\r\n$$\\text{Area}(\\Delta ADE) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AD \\times EF$$\r\n$$\\text{Area}(\\Delta BDE) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times DB \\times EF$$\r\n$$\\frac{\\text{Area}(\\Delta ADE)}{\\text{Area}(\\Delta BDE)} = \\frac{AD}{DB} \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$$\r\n\r\nSimilarly:\r\n$$\\frac{\\text{Area}(\\Delta ADE)}{\\text{Area}(\\Delta DEC)} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2} \\times AE \\times DG}{\\frac{1}{2} \\times EC \\times DG} = \\frac{AE}{EC} \\quad \\text{--- (2)}$$\r\n\r\nSince $\\Delta BDE$ and $\\Delta DEC$ lie on the same base $DE$ and between the same parallels $DE \\parallel BC$:\r\n$$\\text{Area}(\\Delta BDE) = \\text{Area}(\\Delta DEC) \\quad \\text{--- (3)}$$\r\n\r\nFrom (1), (2), and (3):\r\n$$\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC}.$$\r\nHence proved. $\\blacksquare$	t	2025	Official SQP	t	MATH	All India
CBSE_SQP_2025_Q14	M10_CH05	Renewable Energy Panel Array Progression Model	Standard	A solar power company installs photovoltaic panels in sequential rows. The first row contains $14$ panels, and each subsequent row contains $4$ more panels than the preceding row. The installation contains $25$ rows in total.\r\n(i) How many solar panels are installed in the 15th row? (1 Mark)\r\n(ii) What is the number of panels in the final 25th row? (1 Mark)\r\n(iii) Calculate the total number of solar panels installed across all 25 rows. (2 Marks)	[{"step": "(i) a15 = a + 14d = 14 + 14(4) = 14 + 56 = 70 panels", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "(ii) a25 = a + 24d = 14 + 24(4) = 14 + 96 = 110 panels", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "(iii) S25 = (25/2)[14 + 110] = (25/2)*124 = 25 * 62 = 1,550 panels", "marks": 2.0}]	4.0	Case Study	Applying	Medium	\N	["CBSE_SQP_2025", "Official_Sample_Paper", "Section_E", "Case_Study"]	The installation forms an A.P.:\r\n• First term $a = 14$\r\n• Common difference $d = 4$\r\n• Total rows $n = 25$\r\n\r\n(i) Panels in the 15th row ($a_{15}$):\r\n$$a_{15} = a + 14d = 14 + 14(4) = 14 + 56 = 70\\text{ panels}.$$\r\n\r\n(ii) Panels in the 25th row ($a_{25}$):\r\n$$a_{25} = a + 24d = 14 + 24(4) = 14 + 96 = 110\\text{ panels}.$$\r\n\r\n(iii) Total solar panels across all 25 rows ($S_{25}$):\r\n$$S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + l)$$\r\n$$S_{25} = \\frac{25}{2}(14 + 110) = \\frac{25}{2} \\times 124 = 25 \\times 62 = 1550\\text{ panels}.$$	t	2025	Official SQP	t	MATH	All India
CBSE_SQP_2025_Q15	M10_CH12	Hemispherical Dome Glass Architecture Surface Area Model	Standard	An ecological botanical nursery is built in the form of a cylinder of diameter $14\\text{ m}$ and height $4\\text{ m}$, surmounted by a hemispherical glass dome of radius $7\\text{ m}$.\r\n(i) Find the surface area of the cylindrical base wall. (Take $\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}$) (1 Mark)\r\n(ii) Find the surface area of the hemispherical glass dome. (1.5 Marks)\r\n(iii) Calculate the total internal air volume enclosed by the nursery structure. (1.5 Marks)	[{"step": "(i) Cylinder CSA = 2*pi*r*h = 2*(22/7)*7*4 = 176 m^2", "marks": 1.0}, {"step": "(ii) Hemisphere CSA = 2*pi*r^2 = 2*(22/7)*49 = 308 m^2", "marks": 1.5}, {"step": "(iii) Total Volume = Cylinder Vol + Hemisphere Vol = pi*r^2*h + (2/3)*pi*r^3 = (22/7)*49*4 + (2/3)*(22/7)*343 = 616 + 718.67 = 1334.67 m^3", "marks": 1.5}]	4.0	Case Study	Applying	Medium	\N	["CBSE_SQP_2025", "Official_Sample_Paper", "Section_E", "Case_Study"]	Given: Radius $r = 7\\text{ m}$, Cylinder Height $h = 4\\text{ m}$.\r\n\r\n(i) Curved Surface Area of the cylindrical wall:\r\n$$\\text{CSA}_{\\text{cylinder}} = 2\\pi r h = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 4 = 176\\text{ m}^2.$$\r\n\r\n(ii) Surface Area of the hemispherical glass dome:\r\n$$\\text{CSA}_{\\text{hemisphere}} = 2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 308\\text{ m}^2.$$\r\n\r\n(iii) Total volume enclosed:\r\n$$V = V_{\\text{cylinder}} + V_{\\text{hemisphere}} = \\pi r^2 h + \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3$$\r\n$$= \\pi r^2 \\left(h + \\frac{2}{3}r\\right) = \\left(\\frac{22}{7} \\times 49\\right) \\left(4 + \\frac{14}{3}\\right)$$\r\n$$= 154 \\times \\left(\\frac{26}{3}\\right) = \\frac{4004}{3} \\approx 1334.67\\text{ m}^3.$$	t	2025	Official SQP	t	MATH	All India
SCI_2022_AI_03	S10_CH09	\N	Standard (041)	A cross between two tall pea plants resulted in offspring having a few dwarf plants. What must be the genotype of both parent plants?\r\n(A) TT and TT\r\n(B) Tt and Tt\r\n(C) TT and Tt\r\n(D) Tt and tt	{"answer": "1 Mark for Option (B)"}	1.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	1f208168246a0d6501939fb4742c7994d4d3316a10130edadca007bb42b27508	[]	Correct Option: (B)\r\nTt and Tt. For dwarf offspring (tt) to appear, both parents must contribute a recessive "t" allele.	t	2022	All India Set 1	f	SCI	All India
