SCI_2022_AI_15	S10_CH08	\N	Standard (041)	(a) Differentiate between self-pollination and cross-pollination.\r\n(b) What are sexually transmitted infections (STIs)? Name one bacterial STI and one viral STI, and state the primary method of prevention.	{"stis": "2.5 Marks", "pollination": "2.5 Marks"}	5.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	f19ed23992d16f02ba0d5d9029fd50a36f13c9875f118c8514828b7f13e48cde	[]	(a) Differences:\r\n- Self-Pollination: Pollen transfers from anther to stigma of the same flower or another flower on the same plant; external pollinators are not required; produces less genetic variation.\r\n- Cross-Pollination: Pollen transfers from anther to stigma of a flower on a different plant of the same species; requires external agents (wind, insects, water); introduces genetic diversity.\r\n(b) STIs:\r\n- Definition: Infectious diseases transmitted primarily through sexual contact.\r\n- Bacterial STI: Gonorrhea (or Syphilis).\r\n- Viral STI: Genital Warts (HPV) or HIV-AIDS.\r\n- Prevention: Consistent use of barrier methods (condoms) and avoiding unprotected intercourse with multiple partners.	t	2022	All India Set 1	f	SCI	All India
