PYQ_2024_BASIC_SET1_Q01	M10_CH01	Prime Factor Decomposition	Basic	The prime factorisation of natural number $140$ is:\r\n(A) $2 \\times 5 \\times 7$\r\n(B) $2^2 \\times 5 \\times 7$\r\n(C) $2^3 \\times 5$\r\n(D) $2 \\times 7^2$	[{"step": "Divide 140 step-by-step: 140/2 = 70, 70/2 = 35, 35/5 = 7", "marks": 0.5}, {"step": "Express as 2^2 * 5 * 7 and select Option (B)", "marks": 0.5}]	1.0	Objective	Remembering	Easy	\N	["CBSE_2024", "Basic_241", "Set_1", "Section_A"]	Performing prime factorisation:\r\n$$140 = 2 \\times 70 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 35 = 2^2 \\times 5 \\times 7$$\r\nTherefore, Option **(B)** is correct.	t	2024	Basic Set 1	t	MATH	All India
PYQ_2024_BASIC_SET1_Q02	M10_CH02	Number of Zeroes from Graph Intersections	Basic	The graph of $y = P(x)$ intersects the $x$-axis at $3$ distinct points and touches it at $1$ other point. The total number of zeroes of $P(x)$ is:\r\n(A) $3$\r\n(B) $4$\r\n(C) $2$\r\n(D) $1$	[{"step": "State rule: each point where graph intersects or touches x-axis corresponds to a real zero", "marks": 0.5}, {"step": "Total points on x-axis = 3 + 1 = 4 zeroes (Option B)", "marks": 0.5}]	1.0	Objective	Understanding	Easy	\N	["CBSE_2024", "Basic_241", "Set_1", "Section_A"]	The real zeroes of a polynomial $y = P(x)$ correspond to the coordinates where its curve intersects or touches the $x$-axis ($y = 0$).\r\nTotal points on $x$-axis $= 3\\text{ (crossings)} + 1\\text{ (tangent touch)} = 4$.\r\nTherefore, the number of zeroes is **4** (Option B).	t	2024	Basic Set 1	t	MATH	All India
