SST_2017_D_02	SS10_HIS_02	\N	Standard (041)	Why was the Round Table Conference in London boycotted by the Indian National Congress in 1930?\r\n(A) Congress leaders demanded complete independence (Purna Swaraj) and were imprisoned during Civil Disobedience\r\n(B) The British increased salt taxes further\r\n(C) Simon Commission had not arrived\r\n(D) Jallianwala Bagh inquiries were dropped	{"answer": "1 Mark for Option (A)"}	1.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	8033ad45d8cb8c0fb96970cece9981cf51828d9c34ac958e99709daf1b1e4744	[]	Correct Option: (A)\r\nCongress boycotted the First Round Table Conference because most leaders were jailed during the Civil Disobedience Movement and the British refused to accept immediate Purna Swaraj.	t	2017	Delhi Set 1	f	SST	Delhi
