SST_2017_AI_04	SS10_POL_01	\N	Standard (041)	In Belgium, power was shared equally between which two major linguistic groups in the central government?\r\n(A) Dutch-speaking and French-speaking ministers\r\n(B) German-speaking and Dutch-speaking ministers\r\n(C) French-speaking and English-speaking ministers\r\n(D) Walloon and Fleming ethnic leaders	{"answer": "1 Mark for Option (A)"}	1.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	2bc05af28c3140cc454082a74a4ca4cffeca7739a6407caf9463888b54fb8f6d	[]	Correct Option: (A)\r\nThe Belgian Constitution mandates that the number of Dutch-speaking and French-speaking ministers shall be equal in the central government.	t	2017	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
SST_2017_AI_05	SS10_ECO_01	\N	Standard (041)	Explain why national development should balance economic income with social indicators like healthcare and education.	{"explanation": "2 Marks"}	2.0	Board Exam	\N	Board Standard	45023d83df8b14a6cddfd39a9376a8aca94d2517239f654cd834d6b418f7f142	[]	Economic income provides purchasing power for material goods, but quality of life depends on non-material factors such as life expectancy, low infant mortality, basic education, personal security, and clean environments. High per capita income without public healthcare or schooling fails to support sustainable human development.	t	2017	All India Set 1	f	SST	All India
